          "type": "answer",
          "text": "Great! Premises are the statements in an argument that provide reasons, evidence, or support for the conclusion. They are the 'because' part \u2014 the foundation the conclusion rests on. An argument can have one premise or many. The key question is always: what statements are being offered as reasons to believe the conclusion?"
