          "type": "answer",
          "text": "Perfect! Propositional logic (also called sentential logic) studies how entire propositions can be combined and related using logical operators like AND, OR, NOT, and IF-THEN. Instead of breaking statements down into subjects and predicates (like categorical logic), propositional logic treats whole statements as the basic units and studies their combinations. Why it matters in business: Every strategic decision, investment memo, and marketing claim has a logical structure. Propositional logic helps you: (1) Symbolize complex arguments to see their structure clearly. (2) Test arguments for validity using truth tables. (3) Spot logical errors in reasoning. (4) Clarify what exactly is being claimed.",
