        "hint": "Think about: sample size, sampling method (random or self-selected?), control groups, blinding, whether the measure is valid, who funded the study, and whether the conclusion matches what was actually measured.",
        "follow_up": "Excellent questions. Now, a key distinction: is the 30% more energy claim — based on going from 5.2 to 6.8 on a 10-point scale — an accurate way to present the data? Is it a percentage increase, or a percentage-point increase? Why does this distinction matter?"
