    "title": "Resource: Guide to writing good operational definitions",
    "content": "For the PBL project, you'll be writing precise replacements for vague marketing claims. Here's a quick framework for operational definitions — definitions that specify measurable criteria:\n\n1. Define the concept (what are we measuring?)\n2. Specify the unit of measurement (percentage? mg? minutes? dollars?)\n3. Set the comparison baseline (compared to what?)\n4. State the methodology (how was this measured/verified?)\n\nExample: Instead of \"deeply hydrating,\" try \"increases skin moisture by 35% after 4 weeks (measured via corneometer, n=50 participants, vs. untreated control).\"\n\nShare other good (or bad) definitions you've found in the wild!",
